e\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:386:    Simplify a list of channels by reducing null bits, merging identical signatures, and absorbing subsets.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:388:    :param channels: List of input channels.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:389:    :type channels: list[Channel]\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:390:    :param max_bits: Maximum number of bits allowed per simplified channel, defaults to 4.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:394:    :return: Simplified list of channels.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:397:    channels = reduce_null_bits(channels, null_col_id)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:398:    channels = normalize_channels(channels)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:399:    channels = merge_identical_channels(channels)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:400:    channels = absorb_subset_channels(channels, max_bits)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:401:    return channels\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:405:    \"\"\"Samples from multiple error channels and transforms to a reduced basis.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:407:    This class combines multiple error channels (each producing error bits e0, e1, ...)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:416:    2. Merging channels with identical column signatures, i.e. channels whose corresponding\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:418:    3. Absorbing channels whose signatures are subsets of others, i.e. channels whose corresponding\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:419:        columns in error_transform are a strict subset of another channel's columns.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:422:        >>> probs = [error_probs(0.1), error_probs(0.2)]  # two 1-bit channels\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:431:        channel_probs: list[Any],\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:435:        \"\"\"Initialize the sampler with channel probabilities and a basis transformation.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:438:            channel_probs: List of probability arrays. Channel i has shape (2^k_i,)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:440:                For example, if channels have shapes [(4,), (2,), (4,)], they\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:458:        channels: list[Channel] = []\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:460:        for probs in channel_probs:\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:463:            channels.append(Channel(probs=probs, unique_col_ids=col_ids))\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:466:        self.channels = simplify_channels(channels, null_col_id=null_col_id)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:473:            self.channels, self.signature_matrix\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:475:        self._jax_data = self._precompute_jax(self.channels, self.signature_matrix)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:489:        channels: list[Channel], signature_matrix: Any\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:492:        Precompute per-channel data for geometric-skip sampling.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:494:        :param channels: List of error channels.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:495:        :type channels: list[Channel]\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:502:        for ch in channels:\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:526:        Sample from all error channels and transform to the f-basis.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:559:        channels: list[Channel], signature_matrix: Any\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:564:        channels.  log_probs_padded has shape (num_channels, max_outcomes) and\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:565:        xor_patterns_padded has shape (num_channels, max_outcomes, num_f).\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:572:        for ch in channels:\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:596:        # Pad all channels to the same number of outcomes\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:613:            jnp.array(np.stack(log_probs_list)),  # (num_channels, max_outcomes)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:614:            jnp.array(np.stack(xor_pats_list)),  # (num_channels, max_outcomes, num_f)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:618:        \"\"\"Sample from all error channels on-device using JAX categorical sampling.\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:648:    num_channels = log_probs_all.shape[0]\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/noise_model.py:649:    subkeys = jax.random.split(key, num_channels)\n/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/zx/stabilizertcircuit.py:137:        self._ch